would do once you confirm)\n- Action: Delete messages (move to Trash) that match all of:\n  - Label = \"Newsletters\"\n  - Message date older than 1 year from today (i.e., before 2025-09-05)\n- Scope: every message with that label and older than 2025-09-05. (I will delete messages, not whole calendar events.)\n- How deletion works / visibility: messages will be moved to your Gmail Trash. They will not be emailed to anyone; only your account is affected.\n- Reversibility: messages in Trash can be restored for up to ~30 days; after that they are permanently removed by Google and typically not recoverable.\n- What could go wrong: I might delete newsletters you still want (including ones with useful attachments or receipts), or messages you’ve starred/flagged; if a conversation contains both old newsletter messages and newer important messages, removing the old messages could be confusing.\n\nOptions to change before I act\n- Instead of deleting, I can archive them (keeps them searchable but removes them from the label view? — note: archiving won’t remove the custom label; tell me if you prefer removing the label instead).\n- Exclude starred messages, messages from specific senders, or messages with attachments.\n- Preview: I can show you the oldest 10–20 newsletter threads/messages for quick approval before bulk deletion.\n\nPlease confirm exactly:\n1) Proceed to delete all messages with label \"Newsletters\" dated before 2025-09-05? (yes / no)\n2) If yes, do you want to exclude starred messages or any senders, or would you like a preview first? (specify)\n3) Delete (move to Trash) vs Archive vs Remove label (choose one)\n\nOnce you reply with explicit confirmation and any exclusions, I will proceed.","type":"output_text"}],"id":"msg_0d6303bdf7abbb85016a9c9b8143bc87d0a6f62102474b5f78","role":"assistant","status":"completed","type":"message"}],"parallel_tool_calls":true,"presence_penalty":0.0,"previous_response_id":null,"prompt_cache_key":null,"prompt_cache_retention":"